431:*The certificate.* If $R_T(I) \subseteq V$ and $m(v) > 0$ for all $v \in V$, Lemma {@lem-argmax} gives $f = T$ on $V \supseteq R_T(I)$, and sufficiency, which did not use injectivity, applies.
473:With $e^{c} = 2N + 5$ instead, the same computation gives a decoder that passes both rows and is exact under unpinned decoding on every input of length at most $N$, yet wrong on $\mathsf a^{N+2}$ (`no_finite_check`); testing every input up to a given length does not suffice either. Conversely, if the context moves every logit by at most $\tau$ from the logit at the pinned row and every certified margin exceeds $2\tau$, unpinned decoding is exact on every input (`unpinned_exact_of_close`). In the construction, the head's write is such a perturbation, and it grows without bound.
486:A transcript makes $K$ calls. Call $i$ receives the input $x_i = q_i(r_{<i})$ and returns $r_i = E_i(x_i)$, where $E_i$ is the procedure that executes it and $r_{<i} = (r_1, \dots, r_{i-1})$; the answer $g(r)$ reads only $r = (r_1, \dots, r_K)$. Call $i$ has a table $T_i$, the function its procedure is certified to compute. The intended computation has inputs $q^*_i$, functions $T^*_i$ and combining program $g^*$, with results $r^*_i = T^*_i(q^*_i(r^*_{<i}))$ and answer $g^*(r^*)$.
506:(b) Under the hypothesis, (a) places the event $\{g(r) \neq g^*(r^*)\}$ inside the union of the other three, and the bound follows from monotonicity and subadditivity of $\mu$, which hold for arbitrary sets, so no measurability is needed; a probability distribution gives ({@eq-compose}). For a procedure certified on the views it reaches, the hypothesis $E_i(x_i) = T_i(x_i)$ is Theorem {@thm-p} applied to its run on $x_i$, whatever the length of $x_i$ and the order of the calls. In Lean, (a) is proved for arbitrary $E_i$, $T_i$ and $T^*_i$, and (b) for calls executed by sheet procedures (`Sketchpad.sheet_error_bound`) and by the token-form procedure (`error_bound`), with the hypothesis derived from Theorem {@thm-p} in each form (`Sketchpad.sheet_compose_exact`, `compose_exact`).
511:A certificate is a JSON file distributed with the model graph. It specifies the prompt forms under which it was measured, the numerical precision of each graph, the library version, hashes of the glyph set and of every model file, the device and the time, and, for each table, the number of rows, the number passed and every row's margin in a fixed order, to $10^{-3}$ logits. A client accepts a certificate only if every hash matches the loaded files, and recomputes the lowest-margin tenth of each table before use.
515:Every number in this paper is listed, with its source record, in `paper/numbers.md` of the Sketchpad repository. Training, server certification, the gate identity test and dialogue fine-tuning are scripted for Modal; the device certificate and browser test run in the client; the algebra tests and cost tables run with `pnpm vitest run src/lib/sketchpad/program`; the comparison is in `paper/baselines/`; the Lean proofs build with `lake build` in `paper/lean/`, and `lake env lean Paper.lean`, run in the same folder, prints the axioms of every statement.

